Description: Lock a precision scroll to one direction when horizontal tab scrolling is disabled
 GTK runs only the first scroll controller that handles an event, so during a
 slightly diagonal touchpad or TrackPoint scroll the vertical handler takes the
 events with a vertical part and the horizontal handler gets the events whose
 vertical part is 0. With gtk-horizontal-tab-scroll disabled, those were sent
 to the program as whole columns of horizontal scrolling in between.
 .
 With horizontal tab scrolling disabled, each precision scroll (from GTK's
 scroll-begin to scroll-end) is now locked to one direction, decided on its
 first event: vertical without mouse reporting, where the terminal has no
 second direction; otherwise the larger part of that event. The other direction
 is dropped until the scroll ends. Mouse wheels and enabled tab scrolling are
 unchanged.
